@main
TOS Mutexes

Binary locks built on ll/sc atomic instructions.
A mutex is a single i64: 0 = unlocked, 1 = locked.
Threads that cannot acquire the mutex yield and retry.
@

  import services.*

  extern atomic_dec_if_positive(addr: *i64) -> i64
  extern atomic_inc(addr: *i64)

@api mutex_init(m) — Initialize a mutex to unlocked state.

  mutex_init(m: *i64)
      *m = 1

@tech
The mutex is modeled as a binary semaphore: value 1 means
unlocked (one permit available), value 0 means locked.
mutex_lock decrements atomically; mutex_unlock increments.
@

@api mutex_lock(m) — Acquire the mutex, yielding until available.

  mutex_lock(m: *i64)
      while atomic_dec_if_positive(m) == 0
          yield()

@api mutex_unlock(m) — Release the mutex.

  mutex_unlock(m: *i64)
      atomic_inc(m)

@api mutex_trylock(m) -> i64 — Non-blocking acquire. Returns 1 on success, 0 on failure.

  mutex_trylock(m: *i64) -> i64
      atomic_dec_if_positive(m)
